the summer of 2008 Commerce Bank has big  plans for the future its directors want  to take over Germany's third largest  financial institution the drezna bank  for nine billion euros but then the  financial crisis hits commercial banks  share prices go into freefall but it's  too late to stop the takeover the  purchase and losses caused by the crash  drive the back to the edge of bankruptcy  the German government has to step in  Commerce Bank receives over 16 billion  euros in state funds and is partially  nationalized its share price recovered  slightly the bank wants full  independence back as soon as possible  in April 2011 it pays the government  back fourteen point three billion euros  of the money owes but the bank shares  are now penny stocks  and the ECB's fitness test show Commerce  Bank is low on capital to stock up its  war chest it has to issue fresh stock  but companies which share prices under  Euro can't do that so the bank gets  around the rule by bundling ten shares  into one and selling them as a package  that raises the share price tenfold  although the improvement is largely on  paper
 

